-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Midnight Resistance
  Publisher   Ocean, 1990
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Midnight Resistance (1990)(Ocean)(128K).z80
  MD5         67bf05d356d51b2b402d88c5f0cdfb21

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz; works on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11). 1.2: the game now holds the original's
              pace: quiet scenes were faster than the original and some busy
              scenes slower.

  Note        Known issues: pace against the original in JNext, 6 runs of 600
              updates with the same input: overall -0.81 to +0.35%, quiet
              scenes -1.59 to +0.73%, busy scenes -0.70 to +0.95% (1.1: quiet
              -9.3 to +1.1%, busy -1.1 to +5.8%); the game waits for a whole
              TV frame each update, so where it is close to a frame boundary
              one update can take a frame more or less than the original, and
              a stretch of 20 game frames can read up to 7% slow or 5% fast.
              Missing: no Enhanced colour set; an earlier build ran on a real
              Next for Dean (2026-10-14), but this one, with the loading
              screen, has not; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite weapons
   3  Infinite backpacks
   4  Infinite keys
   5  Invincible after a death

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

